WEBVTT

00:01.190 --> 00:03.980
Things are just getting weirder and weirder.

00:04.390 --> 00:07.530
I wish they'd all stop abusing 
an old woman like me.

00:07.530 --> 00:10.490
What do they even want me to do?

00:11.660 --> 00:12.740
But...

00:13.140 --> 00:16.990
I guess there are things you can 
only do because your time's short.

00:17.490 --> 00:18.990
Now, then, your ladyship...

00:18.990 --> 00:22.300
I've basically told you everything we know.

00:22.300 --> 00:24.000
Did any of that concern you?

00:24.000 --> 00:27.790
There don't seem to be any huge discrepancies 
from what I've already been told.

00:27.790 --> 00:31.100
But there are a few parts 
that don't make sense to me.

00:32.850 --> 00:38.640
Dolls that move on their own to 
harm others aren't born so easily.

00:38.640 --> 00:42.240
If a renowned doll maker put 
their very soul into the work,

00:42.240 --> 00:45.930
or if a doll was treasured for years 
until it took on its owner's wishes,

00:45.930 --> 00:47.400
I could possibly see it moving...

00:47.400 --> 00:50.410
But the problem is that the person 
who made this wooden doll

00:50.410 --> 00:54.280
is a complete novice, and it was 
only finished a month or so ago.

00:54.680 --> 00:57.910
And the fact that it can shoot 
electricity from its hand is unheard of.

00:57.910 --> 01:01.330
If such a thing could be born 
from an old man's grudge,

01:01.330 --> 01:03.540
this world would be full of even more chaos.

01:03.540 --> 01:05.830
That's the part that's not clicking for me.

01:05.830 --> 01:10.480
I do happen to know someone who just 
may create something as absurd as this.

01:11.270 --> 01:13.490
And if she is the one behind all of this,

01:13.490 --> 01:16.970
dealing with that doll will 
prove to be quite troublesome.

01:18.070 --> 01:19.850
I don't know what all you've got going on,

01:19.850 --> 01:22.100
but I don't think that's the case here.

01:22.100 --> 01:24.850
Zenta's doll is the same as Pinocchio.

01:24.850 --> 01:29.560
There's a special ingredient 
that went into making that doll.

01:29.560 --> 01:31.330
A special ingredient?

01:31.330 --> 01:33.380
Well, in <i>The Adventures of Pinocchio</i>,

01:33.380 --> 01:36.200
he was created from a stick 
that could move and talk.

01:36.200 --> 01:39.470
Well, Zenta didn't have anything like that,

01:39.470 --> 01:41.410
but it's still very special.

01:41.410 --> 01:43.160
A part of that doll was created

01:43.160 --> 01:46.390
with wood from a tree that 
had a meteorite embedded in it.

01:47.370 --> 01:48.610
A mete...

02:54.470 --> 02:57.530
According to Zenta, 
it happened about ten years ago.

02:57.960 --> 03:00.780
He wasn't doing very well at the time.

03:00.780 --> 03:03.210
His neuralgia and migraines were pretty bad,

03:03.210 --> 03:06.580
so he went into the mountains, 
contemplating suicide.

03:06.580 --> 03:07.870
And then...

03:17.480 --> 03:21.070
Apparently, Zenta knew immediately 
that it was a meteorite.

03:21.070 --> 03:25.300
It's quite rare to find a 
meteorite right after it's fallen,

03:25.300 --> 03:28.190
and it would've made the news 
if he'd let the public know.

03:28.190 --> 03:31.690
But Zenta felt a strange allure from it,

03:31.690 --> 03:34.940
so he took the branch home 
and kept it by his side.

03:34.940 --> 03:40.500
And then, amazingly, 
his condition started to improve.

03:41.270 --> 03:46.660
From then on, Zenta was infatuated 
with the branch and took good care of it.

03:46.660 --> 03:50.170
Since ancient times, meteorites were regarded 
as mysterious objects from the sky,

03:50.170 --> 03:52.330
and were occasionally even worshiped.

03:52.330 --> 03:54.410
They were considered messages from heaven,

03:54.410 --> 03:58.230
and were even placed in 
shrines as signs of miracles.

03:58.230 --> 04:00.460
But meteorites are just meteorites.

04:00.460 --> 04:02.620
They don't exactly have powers to move dolls

04:02.620 --> 04:05.470
or get them to shoot 
electricity from their hands.

04:05.470 --> 04:10.250
The earth has the power to create yokai, 
ayakashi, ghosts, and demons,

04:10.250 --> 04:13.980
all of which bring about mysterious 
phenomena for many people.

04:13.980 --> 04:17.520
There may well be a similar kind 
of power in outer space, as well.

04:17.520 --> 04:19.420
And it's possible that power 
inhabits meteorites,

04:19.420 --> 04:22.730
falls down to earth, takes on 
the wishes of the one who finds it,

04:22.730 --> 04:24.990
and causes potential harm.

04:24.990 --> 04:27.490
It's basically a cosmic 
supernatural phenomenon.

04:27.900 --> 04:28.980
Ah...

04:30.620 --> 04:35.040
Most just laughed at Zenta's 
story about the meteorite,

04:35.040 --> 04:37.040
but he was serious about it.

04:38.420 --> 04:41.420
Do you think you can 
make a doll to replace him?

04:41.420 --> 04:44.370
Just because you have a special 
tree branch like from Pinocchio,

04:44.370 --> 04:47.820
do you really think that thing's 
gonna start moving, too?

04:49.660 --> 04:52.930
This stone makes wishes come true.

04:52.930 --> 04:57.940
The old man who created Pinocchio 
went through hell because of him.

04:58.370 --> 05:01.470
Nothing good's gonna come 
of making that thing.

05:02.940 --> 05:06.070
Well, I've already been through hell.

05:06.070 --> 05:09.760
The arm that has the meteorite 
infused in it is the right arm.

05:09.760 --> 05:12.700
That's probably why it can only shoot 
electricity from its right hand.

05:12.700 --> 05:13.950
Tae-san!

05:13.950 --> 05:17.380
That's the first time I've heard about this!

05:17.380 --> 05:19.630
Would it have done any good if I had?

05:20.010 --> 05:23.300
If we knew about that, we wouldn't 
have tried to attack it so carelessly!

05:23.300 --> 05:26.980
There's no way we stand a chance 
against a cosmic supernatural being!

05:26.980 --> 05:30.050
Well, I didn't know what you lot 
were dealing with, either.

05:30.050 --> 05:34.980
Must be rough for you, having to 
deal with cosmically divine beings.

05:34.980 --> 05:37.060
You need to help me out, Senpai!

05:37.060 --> 05:40.480
Anything from outer space 
is a foreign body to this land.

05:40.480 --> 05:43.500
It probably will not agree 
with the order of this world.

05:43.500 --> 05:45.570
We must get rid of it immediately.

05:45.570 --> 05:49.280
This situation is much more understandable 
than it would be if she was involved.

05:49.280 --> 05:53.370
Did Zenta-san make any mention 
of what he planned on doing

05:53.370 --> 05:55.210
with the doll while he was making it?

05:55.210 --> 05:56.290
No.

05:56.290 --> 05:58.400
I see.

05:58.400 --> 06:02.670
So he didn't clearly state that he was 
making the doll with Pinocchio in mind.

06:03.650 --> 06:05.600
What of it?

06:05.600 --> 06:06.420
Oh!

06:06.420 --> 06:10.930
When the doll was getting close 
to completion, Zenta did say...

06:10.930 --> 06:17.730
This might be able to 
fulfill my wishes in my place.

06:18.750 --> 06:23.610
If only I had realized what Zenta 
was trying to do back then...

06:23.610 --> 06:26.580
It would've been impossible to realize 
that with so little information.

06:26.580 --> 06:31.310
Even I couldn't fathom a doll starting 
to move and having that much power.

06:32.240 --> 06:33.990
But it was quite careless.

06:33.990 --> 06:37.730
Eventually, the people from town 
would've seen that thing.

06:37.730 --> 06:42.460
Even if they were scared at first, they'd 
all band together to destroy that thing.

06:42.460 --> 06:46.180
And how many victims would 
result from that electricity then?

06:47.410 --> 06:49.090
So what will you do, our lady?

06:49.090 --> 06:53.260
You don't look strong enough 
to destroy that thing.

06:53.260 --> 06:54.470
T-Tae-san!

06:54.470 --> 06:56.710
Our lady is our goddess of wisdom.

06:56.710 --> 07:00.390
Of course she doesn't seem suited to violence.

07:00.390 --> 07:03.390
And this time, Kuro-dono is here!

07:03.390 --> 07:06.820
He is more monstrous than any monster alive.

07:06.820 --> 07:10.200
He could wallop that doll in a single blow!

07:11.970 --> 07:14.550
This scrawny little boy?

07:14.550 --> 07:16.140
Right?

07:16.140 --> 07:20.080
Excuse me! Kuro-senpai is my boyfriend, 
and he has my parents' approval!

07:20.080 --> 07:22.670
Please refrain from insulting him!

07:22.670 --> 07:24.420
Oh, your boyfriend?

07:24.420 --> 07:27.120
I'm not sure if "boyfriend" is the right word.

07:27.120 --> 07:28.340
But it's the truth!

07:28.340 --> 07:29.760
And what issue do you have

07:29.760 --> 07:32.370
with having a cute maiden 
like myself as your girlfriend?

07:32.370 --> 07:36.350
I'm not sure you should be calling yourself 
a maiden when you'll be twenty soon.

07:36.350 --> 07:39.880
Well, thanks to you, Senpai, 
I'm a maiden no longer.

07:40.680 --> 07:43.450
I couldn't care less about your relationship.

07:43.450 --> 07:46.320
So as long as he's here, 
we can stop that doll, right?

07:47.360 --> 07:52.200
Even if Kuro-senpai wasn't here, 
destroying the doll would be simple.

07:52.200 --> 07:54.430
Did you listen to a word I said?

07:54.430 --> 07:57.830
Even these monsters stood 
no chance with that thing.

07:58.370 --> 08:00.590
The doll hides in the 
mountains during the day

08:00.590 --> 08:02.390
and heads down to the ocean at night,

08:02.390 --> 08:05.170
using almost the same exact route every time.

08:05.170 --> 08:09.300
Then it walks through this beach below us.

08:09.300 --> 08:13.050
And, even if you're near it, 
it won't attack you unless you move.

08:13.050 --> 08:14.300
Right?

08:14.300 --> 08:15.050
Yeah.

08:15.050 --> 08:18.060
Then we just need to wait 
for it, and set a trap.

08:18.410 --> 08:21.430
We'll hide some explosives in the sand,

08:21.430 --> 08:24.960
and when the doll is near 
the center of that trap,

08:24.960 --> 08:26.940
we'll use a remote to set off the explosives,

08:26.940 --> 08:29.110
and the doll will be blown to smithereens.

08:30.230 --> 08:34.530
If explosives are hard to obtain, 
anything flammable would suffice.

08:34.530 --> 08:40.850
We'll just set everything on fire when 
the doll steps in the middle of it.

08:40.850 --> 08:45.420
We can shoot a flaming arrow, 
or throw in a bag of kerosene,

08:45.420 --> 08:47.930
and the doll will literally go up in flames.

08:48.420 --> 08:50.760
It won't have a chance to shoot electricity.

08:50.760 --> 08:52.420
We have this made.

08:54.460 --> 08:57.760
It's so simple. Why didn't it occur to me?

08:57.760 --> 08:59.970
I guess I really am getting old.

08:59.970 --> 09:02.270
You witnessed something otherworldly,

09:02.270 --> 09:05.380
so you likely couldn't think of 
anything more grounded anymore.

09:05.380 --> 09:06.690
I can't blame you.

09:06.690 --> 09:08.560
What a mess.

09:08.560 --> 09:12.530
Just a little more thought, and it 
would've been easy to destroy that doll.

09:12.530 --> 09:15.150
That's exactly why it doesn't make sense.

09:15.150 --> 09:17.340
What do you mean?

09:17.340 --> 09:20.530
That doll is supposed to be 
something Zenta-san made for revenge

09:20.530 --> 09:22.540
after his grandson was killed, right?

09:22.910 --> 09:26.110
It's supposed to be Zenta-san's 
curse in physical form.

09:26.110 --> 09:28.540
But then, isn't it strange?

09:28.540 --> 09:33.860
Wouldn't the doll then go straight 
to the person who killed his grandson?

09:34.590 --> 09:36.630
You're right!

09:36.630 --> 09:40.460
The four college students 
in that car were arrested,

09:40.460 --> 09:43.770
but the only one indicted was the driver.

09:42.180 --> 09:43.770
<b>Not indicted</b>

09:42.180 --> 09:43.770
<b>Indicted</b>

09:42.180 --> 09:43.770
<b>Not indicted</b>

09:42.180 --> 09:43.770
<b>Not indicted</b>

09:43.770 --> 09:47.430
Though apparently, there were testimonies 
saying that they were messing around,

09:43.770 --> 09:52.150
<b>Not indicted</b>

09:43.770 --> 09:52.150
<b>Indicted</b>

09:43.770 --> 09:52.150
<b>Not indicted</b>

09:43.770 --> 09:52.150
<b>Not indicted</b>

09:47.430 --> 09:52.170
disrupting the driver, and didn't 
try to act to help the victim.

09:52.170 --> 09:57.150
And the one who was indicted had 
rich parents who paid off the damages,

09:57.150 --> 10:01.910
and then he was released, 
due to his remorse for his crime.

10:02.300 --> 10:04.250
I'm not sure if it can be said that

10:04.250 --> 10:06.720
they paid the price in the 
eyes of the victim's family,

10:06.720 --> 10:08.540
considering a child was killed.

10:08.540 --> 10:11.670
Zenta wasn't satisfied.

10:12.070 --> 10:14.580
He resented those college students.

10:15.300 --> 10:18.940
There haven't been any reports of those 
four students dying in strange ways.

10:18.940 --> 10:23.010
Which means that, currently, 
the doll has done nothing to them.

10:23.010 --> 10:26.180
That is strange. How are 
we supposed to take that?

10:26.180 --> 10:28.940
There are plenty of ways to destroy the doll.

10:28.940 --> 10:33.520
That's because Zenta-san made it so that 
the townspeople would be able to destroy it.

10:34.080 --> 10:35.280
In that case...

10:36.380 --> 10:38.400
If the doll is destroyed,

10:38.400 --> 10:41.530
that will definitely bring upon 
a most regrettable result.

10:41.530 --> 10:44.020
Though, I won't let that happen.

10:50.370 --> 10:55.050
<b>Or You Could Wish Upon a Star</b>

11:00.760 --> 11:02.180
You head to the ocean.

11:02.180 --> 11:04.050
All of you, head toward the shore.

11:04.050 --> 11:07.200
Make sure you don't move, 
even if the doll comes near you.

11:07.200 --> 11:08.350
Understood?

11:09.060 --> 11:11.560
What a bizarre sight.

11:16.820 --> 11:20.250
Her ladyship must give you a lot of trouble.

11:20.250 --> 11:21.280
Who knows?

11:21.280 --> 11:26.920
Without her, I may not have known 
how to live my life anymore.

11:28.660 --> 11:31.370
So you can decide a future 
in exchange for your death?

11:31.370 --> 11:33.210
What does that even mean?

11:33.210 --> 11:35.170
Even if I can decide the future,

11:35.170 --> 11:38.900
it's only a future that may actually happen.

11:38.900 --> 11:42.050
I can't reach a future that 
doesn't seem likely to happen.

11:42.050 --> 11:47.870
But you'll at least be able to make the trap
her ladyship sets succeed, no matter what?

11:47.870 --> 11:53.480
Iwanaga would be able to make this 
succeed with her luck alone.

11:53.480 --> 11:58.050
Yeah. I guess that little goddess 
isn't someone you want as your enemy.

11:57.110 --> 11:58.050
Senpai!

12:00.050 --> 12:01.990
The doll has entered the shore.

12:01.990 --> 12:05.080
It should get here in the next few minutes.

12:05.080 --> 12:07.480
Please take your position, Kuro-senpai.

12:07.480 --> 12:13.000
There's a mark over there. 
Please guide the doll over to it.

12:13.000 --> 12:16.150
After that, give us a signal 
at the perfect moment.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.250
Also...

12:18.250 --> 12:20.460
Please try to avoid dying.

12:21.970 --> 12:23.900
You're really saying that now?

12:23.900 --> 12:26.610
Well, it seems the yokai are saying

12:26.610 --> 12:32.600
that no matter how many times you die, 
I seem rather calm and unconcerned.

12:32.600 --> 12:33.860
And that's true.

12:33.860 --> 12:35.630
I'm at least a little concerned!

12:35.630 --> 12:37.890
Even if you'll come right back to life!

12:37.890 --> 12:39.480
Yeah, sure...

12:39.480 --> 12:41.250
Just a little, eh?

12:46.240 --> 12:49.740
Now, then. Let's see how correct you were.

12:49.740 --> 12:53.500
You should always strategize with 
the worst-case scenario in mind.

13:08.290 --> 13:11.450
Since ancient times, 
whether in the East or the West,

13:11.450 --> 13:14.370
dolls were created for the sake of magic.

13:14.370 --> 13:17.050
There are many legends of them being created

13:17.050 --> 13:19.150
as vessels to house gods or spirits.

13:19.150 --> 13:21.990
Some were meant to endure
disasters in a human's place,

13:21.990 --> 13:24.400
or to obey orders to do physical labor.

13:24.400 --> 13:27.280
You even hear about that 
in the story of Pinocchio.

13:27.280 --> 13:30.130
But when you think of dolls and magic,

13:30.130 --> 13:33.610
isn't there something else 
that comes to mind?

13:33.610 --> 13:35.080
D-Don't tell me...

13:35.080 --> 13:37.830
Yes, exactly. Cursed dolls.

13:38.190 --> 13:40.670
In the ritual known as the "ox-hour visit,"

13:40.670 --> 13:43.640
a straw doll is nailed to a tree at a shrine

13:43.640 --> 13:45.590
to bring harm to a victim.

13:45.590 --> 13:49.730
Generally, to make a cursed doll work,
you'd attach something related to the victim.

13:49.730 --> 13:51.350
You can attach a drawing or photo of them,

13:51.670 --> 13:56.350
write their name on it, wrap their hair 
around it, or embed their nails into it.

13:56.720 --> 13:59.730
Then the doll becomes the 
very person you want to curse,

13:59.730 --> 14:03.560
and if you stab the doll with nails, 
the victim will feel pain in the same areas.

14:04.360 --> 14:06.490
If you break one of the doll's arms, 
the victim's arm also breaks.

14:06.490 --> 14:10.500
If you set it on fire, the victim 
is supposed to catch fire, as well.

14:11.520 --> 14:14.490
That's what Zenta-san's doll is, too.

14:28.400 --> 14:31.190
Since it moves on its own, 
shoots electricity from its hand,

14:31.190 --> 14:33.260
and is bringing disaster to the town,

14:33.260 --> 14:35.520
it was hard to put all those factors together.

14:35.520 --> 14:38.520
But when you think of it from 
that angle, everything makes sense.

14:59.710 --> 15:03.170
Zenta-san's doll probably 
has something tying it

15:03.170 --> 15:06.550
to the four college students 
who killed his grandson.

15:06.550 --> 15:11.300
If we carelessly destroy the doll, 
the college students will probably die.

15:20.350 --> 15:23.210
Zenta-san had a grudge against 
the four college students

15:23.210 --> 15:25.960
and the people of this town.

15:25.960 --> 15:28.140
But he didn't have the guts to kill someone,

15:28.140 --> 15:30.570
nor the strength to bear 
the responsibility for it.

15:30.870 --> 15:34.090
That's why he thought about 
framing the townspeople

15:34.090 --> 15:35.990
for the deaths of the four college students.

15:36.420 --> 15:38.940
If the doll is what's bringing 
disaster upon this town,

15:38.940 --> 15:41.580
the townspeople will try to destroy it.

15:42.010 --> 15:47.550
A strong hatred over Zenta-san's grandson 
getting killed will come through the doll.

15:47.550 --> 15:49.860
It wasn't just Zenta-san's grudge alone.

15:49.860 --> 15:54.760
It would've manifested the 
hatred of the whole town.

15:54.760 --> 15:58.060
And right around the time 
the doll got destroyed,

15:58.060 --> 16:00.450
the four college students would also die,

16:00.450 --> 16:02.520
and if that news spread throughout the town,

16:02.520 --> 16:06.090
the townspeople would feel 
somehow responsible,

16:06.090 --> 16:08.780
and deep shadows would shroud their hearts.

16:08.780 --> 16:14.280
Zenta-san would also be in the clear 
because he didn't deliver the final blow.

16:14.660 --> 16:18.280
Killing all the fish in the area so that 
the town would go into decline

16:18.280 --> 16:19.790
is quite a curse itself,

16:19.790 --> 16:24.640
but having the townspeople be 
responsible for murder is also a curse.

16:24.640 --> 16:28.310
Being too weak to carry out the crime and 
being a kind-hearted person to begin with

16:28.310 --> 16:30.760
was what brought on this twisted plan.

16:31.170 --> 16:36.140
But in the end, this may be far more 
ominous than any form of retaliation.

16:36.140 --> 16:38.630
What can we do, then?

16:38.630 --> 16:41.930
Are you planning on destroying 
the doll instead of the townspeople,

16:41.930 --> 16:45.060
and shouldering the burden 
of killing those college students?

16:45.060 --> 16:48.070
I don't mind taking the blame or burden,

16:48.070 --> 16:50.940
nor can I say I care what kind 
of tragedy befalls this town.

16:51.710 --> 16:54.150
<i>Such a cold, ruthless attitude 
from such a cute face...</i>

16:54.150 --> 16:58.780
But Zenta-san's actions will throw 
the order of this area into chaos.

16:59.230 --> 17:01.780
Because he's trying to borrow 
the powers of the great beyond

17:01.780 --> 17:04.120
to make his wish come true.

17:04.120 --> 17:06.370
<i>No, her ladyship is...</i>

17:06.370 --> 17:10.250
In that case, we can't 
let that wish come true.

17:10.250 --> 17:12.760
<i>...elegant yet wicked.</i>

17:13.760 --> 17:15.160
There is a way.

17:15.160 --> 17:17.930
If we unbind whatever is 
causing the curse within it,

17:17.930 --> 17:19.850
and then destroy the doll,

17:19.850 --> 17:22.660
disaster won't befall the ones 
who were supposed to be cursed.

17:52.150 --> 17:52.960
Now!

18:26.350 --> 18:28.620
It wasn't difficult to make 
it fall into the hole,

18:29.000 --> 18:35.170
but binding just its right arm would've 
proven difficult without Kuro-senpai's powers.

18:35.170 --> 18:37.860
We might've missed the elbow or the shoulder.

18:37.860 --> 18:40.450
Now go bury it, as we discussed.

18:44.680 --> 18:46.030
Kuro-senpai.

18:47.970 --> 18:49.440
Can you please check the doll

18:49.440 --> 18:53.530
to see if there's anything in it 
binding it to the curse?

18:53.530 --> 18:54.700
Got it.

19:00.010 --> 19:04.200
The hands and feet have parts that connect 
to its joints, and may fall apart easier,

19:04.200 --> 19:06.580
so I think whatever it is 
may be embedded in its torso.

19:08.330 --> 19:11.710
There are a bunch of names of people 
from around here carved in.

19:11.710 --> 19:14.400
The names of the four college students...

19:15.450 --> 19:17.930
and there's one other name.

19:17.930 --> 19:18.970
One other name?

19:21.720 --> 19:23.640
It's mine, isn't it?

19:24.970 --> 19:26.720
Y
